## **11. Agent Skills – Customizing Database Investigation Procedures**

One of the most interesting concepts is that DBAs can customize the investigation methodology using Markdown-based skill files.

The example structure is:

```
sql-server-investigation/
│
├── SKILL.md
│
└── references/
    └── tool-reference.md
```

The `SKILL.md` file defines:

- Skill name and description.
- Incident-triggering conditions.
- Investigation workflow.
- Diagnostic decision paths.
- Severity thresholds.
- Expected report format.

The `tool-reference.md` file contains:

- Health metric thresholds.
- MCP tool parameters.
- Default values.
- SQL Server wait-event mappings.
- Diagnostic reference information.

### **Example: Custom DBA investigation rules**

A DBA team could define the following investigation policy:

| Condition                 | Severity | Investigation                                  |
| ------------------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------- |
| CPU above 80%             | Warning  | Identify top CPU queries                       |
| CPU above 90%             | Critical | Investigate top consumers and plan regressions |
| Blocking above 5 minutes  | Warning  | Identify head blocker                          |
| Blocking above 15 minutes | Critical | Examine blocking chain and transaction         |
| High read latency         | Warning  | Investigate I/O-intensive queries              |
| Query regression          | Warning  | Compare execution plans                        |
| Memory pressure           | Critical | Review memory grants and workload              |

Illustrative DBA thresholds only. These are not universal AWS defaults. Establish thresholds using workload baselines and business SLAs.

The advantage is that investigation procedures can evolve with the database environment without rebuilding the entire agent.

