## **16. Final Thoughts**

The integration of MCP, Agent Skills, and AWS DevOps Agent represents an important development in database operations.

Traditionally, DBAs have relied on monitoring platforms, custom T-SQL scripts, Query Store, Extended Events, and manual investigation procedures.

The new approach connects these capabilities to an AI-driven investigation framework.

The most important architectural concept is the separation of responsibilities:

- CloudWatch identifies abnormal conditions.
- AWS DevOps Agent coordinates investigations.
- Agent Skills define the investigation methodology.
- MCP exposes database diagnostic capabilities.
- AgentCore Gateway controls access to diagnostic tools.
- Lambda executes database queries.
- SQL Server provides the actual diagnostic evidence.

**My conclusion:** AI will not eliminate the need for experienced Database Administrators. However, DBAs who understand database internals, observability, automation, MCP, and agent-based architectures will be better positioned to build the next generation of database operations platforms.

The future DBA role will increasingly combine traditional database engineering with AI-assisted operational intelligence.

